<title>JAPAN: Showa Shell unit plans to start cracker in Nov.</title>
<headline>Showa Shell unit plans to start cracker in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Showa Shell Sekiyu KK said on Wednesday that one of the refiners in its group was scheduled to start full operation of a residue fluid catalytic cracker (RFCC) at its Yokkaichi plant in November.</p>
<p>The cracker, which produces gasoline, gas oil and kerosene from fuel oil, is installed at Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu Co Ltd's 240,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) Yokkaichi plant, in southern Japan.</p>
<p>Test operations of the facility began in July.</p>
<p>Showa Shell Sekiyu K.K. is owned 50 percent by the Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
